`<%- end if %>` on its own line is valid generated Ruby: Erubis (erubis 2.7.0, rails 3.2.12 in Gemfile.lock) emits the statement followed by a newline, and Ruby accepts a modifier `if` whose condition is on the next line, i.e. the next buffer append (always truthy). I reproduced the generated shape: `';  end if 

@output_buffer << '  logo
';` -> `ruby -c` prints `Syntax OK` and it runs, rendering the if/else branch. At most a whitespace chunk is emitted before the branch; no SyntaxError, the view renders. The golden's 'will raise at render' is false.
